## The draft

### Title

```
Make the knowledge base countable: claims, a partial logic, derivation and proofs
```

### Description

````markdown
I had fifty-odd cards that read well and that nobody could check, me
included. Now every card says what it commits to, in a form where two cards
can collide, new statements can be derived, and all of it can be counted.
The number I actually wanted, how much of the base is contradicted, is
still not built. This is everything it stands on. And the project has a
name now: Strange Loops in HyperMarkdown, SLH.

## What changed

**From a sentence to a derived statement.** The text of the cards is
untouched. Each concept card gained a block of claims in its header.

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| 1. Claims | A card is cut into single claims. Each has an address `card#id` that is never reused, an evidence grade and a credence. |
| 2. Formulas | A claim that fits without distortion is written a second time, as `requires(strange-loop, level-crossing)`. The rest stay in words, on purpose. |
| 3. Status | Over all cards a formula is asserted, denied, unsaid or contradicted. A contradiction is a located fact about named claims and makes nothing else derivable. |
| 4. Rules | Nine rules of inference, written as data in a card header, derive formulas nobody wrote. Each one shows its derivation down to the claims. |
| 5. Belief | A credence becomes a cost in bits and costs add along a derivation, so a conclusion built on shaky claims comes out visibly shaky. |
| 6. Proofs | The rules are proved sound in Lean, with no proof left open. |

Beside the pipeline: a score for how far two linked cards disagree, eight
north stars checked as a cover of the base, and the cards read as a typed
graph, checked against a schema that is held in a card of the same graph.

**Names.** Every document indexed under `doc/` is now named
`SLH-<letter>-<id>`: proposal, story, issue, discussion, ledger entry,
memory. Git records each rename as a rename. `doc/memories/` is new, and
every session reads it first. This part touches `doc/`, `.loops/` and
`CLAUDE.md` only: no card, query, script or proof.

## Where it stands

| Measure | Value |
|---|---|
| Claims, on 53 concept cards | 370 |
| Claims that also have a formula | 254 |
| Distinct formulas | 206 |
| Asserted / denied | 122 / 85 |
| Rules of inference | 9 |
| Formulas derived that no claim states | 7 |
| Contradictions between stated formulas | 1 |
| Contradictions reached by derivation | 0 |
| Schema violations in the graph | 0 |
| Claims under no north star | 83 |

**One contradiction in 206 formulas is not good news.** A denial never
starts a derivation, and nearly every `same-as` in the base is a denial, so
about a quarter of the formulas cannot be reached by the rules. The count
says how little the rules can reach, more than how consistent the base is.
Thirteen pairs of cards also contradict each other in their links, where no
formula sees it.

## Not done

- **The health figure is not built.** Nothing computes a share of
  contradicted statements, for the whole base or for a domain. It is what
  this work is for, and it is next. A first reading by hand says it has to
  be a small table of contradiction, coverage and reach, not one
  percentage.
- **No claim graded `proved` is tied to a checked proof.** Lean proves the
  rules of the logic, not the mathematics in the cards.
- **The step from a sentence to a formula is unchecked.** It is a judgment
  made by a model. The check is described, not automated, and the claims
  were not each read against their card by hand.
- **Credences do not move.** Each is still the prior of its evidence grade.
- **A third of the claims have no formula** and are outside the system.
- **Stale prose from the rename.** The issues and the roadmap still speak
  of a `wiki/` vault in running text.

## How to check it

```sh
# the derivation: summary, every derived formula, every contradiction
python3 scripts/derive.py
python3 scripts/derive.py --prove "is-a(godelian-strange-loop, formal-system)"

# the Lean proofs: must build, and no proof may contain `sorry`
cd scripts/lean && lake build

# the schema, the cover by the north stars, the status of each formula
hql run .hql/queries/schema-check.hql
hql run .hql/queries/star-cover.hql
hql run .hql/queries/atom-status.hql
```

`hql` is the query language of HyperMarkDown, built from its own
repository. The first command should report 9 rules, 122 asserted, 85
denied, 7 derived, 1 stated contradiction and 0 derived ones.

